Index: FFmpeg/doc/filters.texi
===================================================================
--- FFmpeg.orig/doc/filters.texi
+++ FFmpeg/doc/filters.texi
@@ -2157,6 +2157,30 @@ agapfill=start=0:max_gap=600
 @end example
 @end itemize
 
+@subsection Commands
+
+This filter supports the following commands:
+@table @option
+@item position
+Report where the output stands, as three numbers with slashes between them:
+the timestamp of the next output sample, the end of the last input frame by
+its own timestamp, both in samples, and the sample rate. The report is empty
+before the first frame.
+
+@item resume
+Continue the output of another agapfill filter. The argument is what the
+@code{position} command of that filter reported. The filter then ignores
+@option{start}, and its first frame is one more step after the other filter's
+last frame: a gap between the two is filled, and any other step is joined.
+The command has no effect once the filter has taken a frame.
+@end table
+
+@command{ffmpeg} builds a new filter graph when the parameters of an input
+change mid-stream, for example the channel layout of the audio. Each agapfill
+filter of the new graph then resumes from the position of the filter in its
+place in the old graph. A filter whose predecessor took no frame starts
+afresh, with @option{start}.
+
